-- the table as data, so that adding a compound costs a line. A row of the table was computed per compound
-- by naming that compound's definitions; here a compound is the inputs themselves -- how many atoms, the
-- generators of its bond-graph symmetries, those of them that also preserve the arrangement at every
-- carbon, the hydrogens an observation counts, and the number of peaks its published spectrum reports --
-- and the two counts are computed inside the tally. The whole table is then one list and one fold, and the
-- extension of it is a list of numbers per compound rather than five definitions.
Compd : Type 0
Compd = (n : Nat) × ((List (Nat → Nat)) × ((List (Nat → Nat)) × ((List Nat) × Nat)))
